cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OmniRAS, please cite the following paper."
title: "OmniRAS: Standardizing Foundation Model Training and Evaluation in Robot-Assisted Surgery"
abstract: >-
  OmniRAS is a family of 1B- and 2B-parameter V-JEPA-2.1 encoders for robot-assisted
  surgery. The work releases two densely annotated robotic-cholecystectomy datasets
  (OmniRAS-PR for phase recognition and a multi-label YT-Chole tool-verb-target task),
  documents continued pretraining at up to 256 compute nodes over roughly 2,650 hours of
  surgical video from 19 sources, and evaluates against raw V-JEPA-2.1 and specialized
  surgical models across six tasks under frozen-encoder and partial fine-tuning regimes.
type: article
year: 2026
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - robot-assisted surgery
  - surgical data science
  - foundation models
  - self-supervised learning
  - V-JEPA
  - surgical phase recognition
  - action triplet recognition
